# 📚 PDF Chatbot — LangChain + Embeddings + ChromaDB

A Streamlit app that lets you upload one or more PDFs and chat with them using
a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) pipeline built with **LangChain**,
**embeddings**, and **ChromaDB** as the vector store.

---

## How It Works (RAG Pipeline)

```
PDF(s) → PyPDFLoader → chunks (RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter)
       → embeddings (OpenAI or local HuggingFace)
       → ChromaDB vector store (persisted to disk)
       → retriever (top-k similarity search)
       → ConversationalRetrievalChain (LLM + chat memory)
       → grounded answer + cited source pages
```

The LLM is instructed (via a strict prompt template) to answer **only** from
retrieved chunks and to say so explicitly if the answer isn't in the document,
rather than falling back on its own general knowledge.

---

## Features

- 📄 Upload **multiple PDFs** at once
- ✂️ Configurable chunk size / overlap
- 🔎 **ChromaDB** vector store, persisted locally (`chroma_db/`) so you don't
  need to re-embed the same PDF every session
- 🧠 Choice of embeddings:
  - **HuggingFace (local, free)** — `all-MiniLM-L6-v2`, no API key required
  - **OpenAI** — `text-embedding-3-small`, higher quality, needs an API key
- 🤖 Choice of chat LLM: **OpenAI** or **Groq**
- 💬 Multi-turn chat with conversation memory
- 📌 **Source page citations** shown under each answer
- 🗑️ One-click "reset knowledge base" to start over with new PDFs

