## Setup

### 1. Clone the repo
```bash
git clone https://github.com/<your-username>/pdf-chatbot-langchain.git
cd pdf-chatbot-langchain
```

### 2. Create a virtual environment
```bash
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate   # Windows: venv\Scripts\activate
```

### 3. Install dependencies
```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### 4. Get an API key (for the chat LLM)
- **OpenAI**: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
- **Groq** (free tier): https://console.groq.com/keys

> Embeddings can run for free locally with HuggingFace — an API key is only
> strictly required for the chat model, and for OpenAI embeddings if you
> choose that option instead.

### 5. Run the app
```bash
streamlit run app.py
```
Opens at `http://localhost:8501`.

---

## Usage

1. Upload one or more PDFs in the **"Upload your PDF(s)"** section.
2. Click **"Process & Index PDFs"** — this chunks the text, embeds it, and
   stores it in a local ChromaDB collection.
3. Enter your LLM API key in the sidebar.
4. Ask questions in the chat box. Each answer includes a **Sources** expander
   showing which page(s) it was drawn from.
5. Use **"Reset knowledge base"** in the sidebar to clear ChromaDB and start
   over with different PDFs.

---

## Design Notes

- **Why ChromaDB?** It's lightweight, runs embedded (no separate server
  needed), and persists to disk — good fit for a local/demo RAG app.
- **Why offer local HuggingFace embeddings?** So the app is fully usable with
  zero API cost/keys for the embedding step; only the chat LLM call needs a
  key.
- **Why a strict "answer only from context" prompt?** To reduce hallucination
  — if retrieval doesn't surface the relevant chunk, the bot says so instead
  of guessing from its own training data.

---

## Known Limitations

- Scanned/image-only PDFs won't extract text (no OCR built in).
- ChromaDB collection is local to the machine running the app — not shared
  across deployments/users out of the box.
- Very large PDFs may take a while to embed on the first run, especially with
  local HuggingFace embeddings on CPU.
- Follow-up questions rely on `ConversationBufferMemory`, which can grow
  large in very long chat sessions.

---

## Tech Stack

- [Streamlit](https://streamlit.io/)
- [LangChain](https://python.langchain.com/) (`langchain`, `langchain-community`,
  `langchain-openai`, `langchain-groq`, `langchain-chroma`)
- [ChromaDB](https://www.trychroma.com/)
- [pypdf](https://pypi.org/project/pypdf/)
- [sentence-transformers](https://www.sbert.net/) for local embeddings

